<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Software and hardware.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train with 4 A100 80GB GPUs using the TRL library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">von Werra et al., 2020</a>)</cite> and Huggingface library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al., 2020</a>)</cite> for full fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ Preference data distribution. ‣ 3.3 Generalization Guarantee ‣ 3 How Well Can GPO Generalize Under Noisy Feedback? ‣ How Well Can Preference Optimization Generalize Under Noisy Feedback?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gradient flow and reward dynamics)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The dynamics of the reward margin for sample <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\dot{r_{j}}(t)=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}\big(f^{\prime}(r_{i}(t))(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,j}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,j})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i}){\Sigma_{ij}}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{r_{j}}(t)=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}\big(f^{\prime}(r_{i}(t))(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,j}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,j})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i}){\Sigma_{ij}}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the time, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the shorthand notation for reward margin of sample <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample covariance matrix with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ij}=g(x_{i})^{\top}g(x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ij}=g(x_{i})^{\top}g(x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is inverse to the learning rate.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider for our theoretical analysis, gradient flow, a continuous approximation of gradient descent.
To follow the reward margins during training, we derive the dynamics of the weight matrix <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> under gradient flow:</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{W}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta\sigma(-\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})^{\top}(W-W_{0})g(x_{i}))(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{W}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta\sigma(-\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})^{\top}(W-W_{0})g(x_{i}))(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> determines the rate of change, where a larger <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a slower rate of change. Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W=W-W_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W=W-W_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, a constant offset from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\Delta\dot{W}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta\sigma(-\underbrace{\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})^{\top}\Delta Wg(x_{i})}_{\text{Reward margin for $x_{i}$}})(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Reward margin for </mtext><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\Delta\dot{W}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta\sigma(-\underbrace{\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})^{\top}\Delta Wg(x_{i})}_{\text{Reward margin for $x_{i}$}})(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which contains the term of the reward margin.
Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\mathbf{y}_{w,j},\mathbf{y}_{l,j},x_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\mathbf{y}_{w,j},\mathbf{y}_{l,j},x_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed, we can consider the flow of the reward margin by multiplying <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,j}-\mathbf{y}_{l,j})^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(\mathbf{y}_{w,j}-\mathbf{y}_{l,j})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> on the left and multiplying <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math> on the right of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\Delta\dot{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\Delta\dot{W}</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields the dynamics for the reward margin:</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{r_{j}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}\sigma(-r_{i}){(\mathbf{y}_{w,j}-\mathbf{y}_{l,j})^{\top}(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})}{\Sigma_{ij}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{r_{j}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}\sigma(-r_{i}){(\mathbf{y}_{w,j}-\mathbf{y}_{l,j})^{\top}(\mathbf{y}_{w,i}-\mathbf{y}_{l,i})}{\Sigma_{ij}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the shorthand notation for reward margin of sample <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the sample covariance matrix with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{ij}=g(x_{i})^{\top}g(x_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{ij}=g(x_{i})^{\top}g(x_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mislabeled von Mises-Fisher Directional Concentration)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given an <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-mislabeled dataset with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 25</annotation></semantics></math> samples, with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\tan(\phi)\leq\sqrt{\log N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\tan(\phi)\leq\sqrt{\log N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the difference between the means of the positively labeled samples and the negatively labeled samples in the noisy dataset has cosine similarity with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> of at least,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We will consider the difference of means between positively labeled samples and negatively labeled samples. We will do so by refactoring this difference as a weighted sum between the mean of noisy positive samples and noisy negative samples.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we consider the distribution of noisy positive samples where each sample can be written as <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is sampled from the positive vMF distribution and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> probability of being 1 and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> probability of being <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by considering the tangential component and lower bounding <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Laforgia &amp; Natalini (2010)</a></cite>, Theorem 1.1, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> has mean lower bounded by
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\gamma}=\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\gamma}=\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, and is bounded between <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have by Hoeffding’s inequality that with probability at least <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{2}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{2}{N}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}\geq(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}\mu_{+}\geq(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Now, we consider the tangential component of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> which is orthogonal to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the tangential component for each <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is distributed uniformly over a <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d-2)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional hypersphere orthogonal to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that norm of the average of the tangential component is upper bounded by <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can ignore the sign from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> due to the symmetry in the uniform distribution. Then, the cosine of the angle between <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is lower bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}}{\sqrt{\left((1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}\right)^{2}+\frac{16}{N^{2}}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}}{\sqrt{\left((1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}\right)^{2}+\frac{16}{N^{2}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">and letting <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\epsilon,\gamma}=(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\epsilon,\gamma}=(1-2\epsilon)\frac{\sqrt{1+\gamma^{2}}-1}{\gamma}-\sqrt{\frac{4\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> and furthering lower bounding the expression gives</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}+\frac{8}{N^{2}t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}+\frac{8}{N^{2}t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and further by</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{8}{N^{2}t_{\epsilon,\gamma}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{8}{N^{2}t_{\epsilon,\gamma}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that this is further lower bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{8}{N\log N}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{8}{N\log N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Then, this occurs with probability at least <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{2}{N}-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{2}{N}-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Following the same argument as above, we have that the cosine of the angle between <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N/2}z_{i}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> where now <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i},x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i},x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> correspond to the noisy negative distribution, is lower bounded by
lower bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{8}{N\log N}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{8}{N\log N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with probability at least <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{2}{N}-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{2}{N}-\frac{4}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will now lower bound the cosine similarity between the difference of means for noisy samples and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> be the average of the noisy positive samples and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> be the average of the noisy negative samples. Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a,b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a,b</annotation></semantics></math> be within <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+},\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+},\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Without loss of generality assume <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|b\right\|&lt;\left\|a\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|b\right\|&lt;\left\|a\right\|</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\frac{\left\|b\right\|}{\left\|a\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\frac{\left\|b\right\|}{\left\|a\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, assume without loss of generality that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}=e_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}=e_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{-}=\cos 2\phi e_{1}+\sin 2\phi e_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{-}=\cos 2\phi e_{1}+\sin 2\phi e_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{1},e_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{1},e_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are the first and second standard basis vectors respectively. Then, we consider the worst case which is when</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=\left\|a\right\|\cos\phi e_{1}+\left\|a\right\|\sin\phi e_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=\left\|a\right\|\cos\phi e_{1}+\left\|a\right\|\sin\phi e_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=r\left\|a\right\|\cos(2\phi+\phi)e_{1}+r\left\|a\right\|\sin(2\phi+\phi)e_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=r\left\|a\right\|\cos(2\phi+\phi)e_{1}+r\left\|a\right\|\sin(2\phi+\phi)e_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Then, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}=\frac{(1+r)(\cos\phi-\cos(2\phi-\phi))}{\sqrt{1+r^{2}-2r\cos(2\phi)}\sqrt{2-2\cos(2\phi)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}=\frac{(1+r)(\cos\phi-\cos(2\phi-\phi))}{\sqrt{1+r^{2}-2r\cos(2\phi)}\sqrt{2-2\cos(2\phi)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Using the half-angle formula and the sum of angles formulas, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}=\frac{(1+r)(\cos\phi\sin\phi-\sin\phi\cos\phi)}{\sqrt{1+r^{2}-2r\cos(2\phi)}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}=\frac{(1+r)(\cos\phi\sin\phi-\sin\phi\cos\phi)}{\sqrt{1+r^{2}-2r\cos(2\phi)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.6" class="ltx_p">In the worst case, using Hoeffding’s inequality and the bound on the tangential component, letting <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\mu}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\mu}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> be the expected radial component, we have that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|a\right\|=(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|a\right\|=(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|b\right\|=(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)-2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|b\right\|=(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)-2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math> so <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 1-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 1-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\epsilon,\gamma}=\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\epsilon,\gamma}=\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}\geq\frac{(2-t_{\epsilon,\gamma})(\cos\phi\sin\phi-\sin\phi\cos\phi)}{\sqrt{2(1-t_{\epsilon,\gamma})(1-\cos(2\phi))+t_{\epsilon,\gamma}^{2}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\langle a-b,\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\rangle}{\left\|a-b\right\|\left\|\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}\right\|}\geq\frac{(2-t_{\epsilon,\gamma})(\cos\phi\sin\phi-\sin\phi\cos\phi)}{\sqrt{2(1-t_{\epsilon,\gamma})(1-\cos(2\phi))+t_{\epsilon,\gamma}^{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.7" class="ltx_p">This is further lower bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{(1-\frac{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}{2})(\cos\phi-\sin\phi\tan\phi)}{\sqrt{1-t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}+t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{(1-\frac{t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}{2})(\cos\phi-\sin\phi\tan\phi)}{\sqrt{1-t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}+t_{\epsilon,\gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.8" class="ltx_p">which is further lower bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}-\frac{1+4\tan\phi}{\sqrt{N\log N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}-\frac{1+4\tan\phi}{\sqrt{N\log N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.9" class="ltx_p">and by the restrictions on <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{4\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}{(1-2\epsilon)l_{\mu}(\gamma)+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}+\frac{4}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.10" class="ltx_p">Lower bounding the result further using that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\mu}(\gamma)\geq\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\mu}(\gamma)\geq\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 25</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}-\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.11" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Training Boundary Shift)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the angle between the boundary at time <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and the initial boundary is at most <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arcsin\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arcsin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arcsin\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the case for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(0)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(0)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f^{\prime\prime}(x)|\leq D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f^{\prime\prime}(x)|\leq D</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. As the weights follow the following dynamics,</p>
<table id="A2.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\Delta\dot{W}=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta f^{\prime}(\underbrace{\beta(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})^{\top}\Delta Wg(x_{i})}_{\text{Reward margin for $x_{i}$}})(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Reward margin for </mtext><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">x</mi><mi mathsize="0.700em">i</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\Delta\dot{W}=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta f^{\prime}(\underbrace{\beta(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})^{\top}\Delta Wg(x_{i})}_{\text{Reward margin for $x_{i}$}})(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">we can say that the initial direction that the weights are along is</p>
<table id="A2.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta f^{\prime}(0)(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mi>β</mi><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta f^{\prime}(0)(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g(x_{i})^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which we will define as <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0+}</annotation></semantics></math>. We aim to control the angle between the initial boundary and the boundary at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. To do so, consider any sample <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> with corresponding reward <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we know that at <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)=\beta({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}W_{0+}g({x}^{*})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)=\beta({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}W_{0+}g({x}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Now, let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0}=({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}W_{0+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0}=({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}W_{0+}</annotation></semantics></math>, and suppose the cosine similarity between <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{0},g(x^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{0},g(x^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than or equal to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)\geq\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)\geq\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Now, we will determine a lower bound, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> which is defined as the first time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)-\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)|=\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)-\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)|=\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, and the lower bound should hold for any sample that satisfies the equation above as this will guarantee that the boundary shifts by at most an angle of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arcsin\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arcsin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arcsin\delta</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. First, we bound the magnitude of the second time derivative of the reward which has the form</p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\ddot{r^{*}}(t)=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime\prime}(r_{i})\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>¨</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>g</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\ddot{r^{*}}(t)=-\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime\prime}(r_{i})\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Since we consider <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with second derivative with magnitude bounded by <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and unit norm embeddings,</p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\ddot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{2\beta^{2}D}{\tau}|\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ddot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{2\beta^{2}D}{\tau}|\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Since we consider time up to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)|\leq 2\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)|\leq 2\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, it follows that</p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\ddot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{4\beta^{3}D\left\|B_{0}\right\|}{\tau^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>¨</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\ddot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{4\beta^{3}D\left\|B_{0}\right\|}{\tau^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Then, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{r^{*}}(t)-\dot{r^{*}}(0)|\leq\frac{4\beta^{3}D\left\|B_{0}\right\|t}{\tau^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{r^{*}}(t)-\dot{r^{*}}(0)|\leq\frac{4\beta^{3}D\left\|B_{0}\right\|t}{\tau^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Then, as we need <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)-\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)|\leq\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(t)-\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}(0)|\leq\beta\left\|B_{0}\right\|\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we can lower bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Then, it follows that for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the angle between the boundary at time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and the initial boundary is at most <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arcsin\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arcsin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arcsin\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of SLiC, since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq x&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq x&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can ensure that the boundary actually stays the same as initialization as long as we stop before any reward is greater than or equal to 1. We can ensure this by bounding <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{r^{*}}(t)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{r^{*}}(t)|</annotation></semantics></math> for any sample <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the fact that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq x&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq x&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and that we will only have rewards in this range, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\dot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{2\beta}{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\dot{r^{*}}(t)|\leq\frac{2\beta}{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then, since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, at any time <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{2\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq\frac{\delta\tau}{2\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(t)\leq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(t)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the boundary will not shift from the initial direction during this range of time. Then, since we set <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\frac{1}{2\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\frac{1}{2\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> for SLiC, this completes the proof. ∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization guarantee under noisy feedback</span>) Under the setup described, suppose we have an <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-mislabeled dataset with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 25</annotation></semantics></math> samples and that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 64</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\delta</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\tan\phi\leq\sqrt{\log N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\tan\phi\leq\sqrt{\log N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq\frac{\sin(\delta)\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq\frac{\sin(\delta)\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is an inverse learning rate and for</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the population risk is bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(2+\gamma)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(2+\gamma)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some constant <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, for any <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,\gamma,\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,\gamma,\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the expected value over the sampled noisy datasets, <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, of the population risk of the model, which we denote by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}_{\epsilon}}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}_{\epsilon}}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}\quad\quad\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}\quad\quad\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start by upper bounding the probability that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}^{\top}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}^{\top}x</annotation></semantics></math> is less than or equal to some value <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z&lt;t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z&lt;t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}=\frac{\sqrt{\gamma^{2}+(1-\frac{3}{d})^{2}}-(1-\frac{3}{d})}{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}=\frac{\sqrt{\gamma^{2}+(1-\frac{3}{d})^{2}}-(1-\frac{3}{d})}{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>. By considering the radial distribution, we know that this is equal to</p>
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\int_{-1}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{\int_{-1}^{1}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\int_{-1}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{\int_{-1}^{1}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the denominator, we can apply Laplace’s method as if we let the exponentiated term be <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dg(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dg(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, we will see that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique maximum and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}(t)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}(t)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the result will have relative error <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math>. Doing so, we have an upper bound of</p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\int_{-1}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\int_{-1}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, we can break the integral on top into two parts</p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\int_{-1}^{0}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt+\int_{0}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>z</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\int_{-1}^{0}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt+\int_{0}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have an upper bound of</p>
<table id="A2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+\int_{0}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>z</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+\int_{0}^{z}e^{\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})}dt}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Then, using that from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa t+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is positive and increasing, we can upper bound the numerator to get</p>
<table id="A2.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1+ze^{\kappa z+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-z^{2})}}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1+ze^{\kappa z+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-z^{2})}}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We can upper bound the expression further by</p>
<table id="A2.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2e^{\kappa z+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-z^{2})}}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2e^{\kappa z+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-z^{2})}}{e^{\kappa t_{0}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}\sqrt{\frac{2\pi(1-t_{0}^{2})^{2}}{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}(1-O(1/d))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.7" class="ltx_p">and we can rewrite this as</p>
<table id="A2.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{2(1-t_{0}^{2})\sqrt{2\pi}}{\sqrt{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}\exp\left(\kappa(z-t_{0})+\frac{d-3}{2}\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2(1-t_{0}^{2})\sqrt{2\pi}}{\sqrt{(d-3)(1+t_{0}^{2})}}\exp\left(\kappa(z-t_{0})+\frac{d-3}{2}\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Then, given <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 64</annotation></semantics></math>, this is upper bounded by</p>
<table id="A2.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(\kappa(z-t_{0})+\frac{d-3}{2}\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(\kappa(z-t_{0})+\frac{d-3}{2}\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.9" class="ltx_p">and further by</p>
<table id="A2.E49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp\left(\frac{d}{2}\left(\gamma(z-t_{0})+\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp\left(\frac{d}{2}\left(\gamma(z-t_{0})+\log\left(\frac{1-z^{2}}{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)\right)(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Then, we are interested in a lower bound for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> which satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma z_{*}+\log(1-z_{*}^{2})=\gamma t_{0}+\log(1-t_{0}^{2})-\frac{2\log(1/B)}{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma z_{*}+\log(1-z_{*}^{2})=\gamma t_{0}+\log(1-t_{0}^{2})-\frac{2\log(1/B)}{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.11" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(\gamma+2)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(\gamma+2)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1-z_{*}^{2})&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-z_{*}^{2})&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, solving</p>
<table id="A2.E51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma z=\gamma t_{0}+\log(1-t_{0}^{2})-\frac{2B}{d}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma z=\gamma t_{0}+\log(1-t_{0}^{2})-\frac{2B}{d}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.12" class="ltx_p">provides a lower bound <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=t_{0}+\frac{\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}{\gamma}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=t_{0}+\frac{\log(1-t_{0}^{2})}{\gamma}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.13" class="ltx_p">Then, using that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}\geq\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}\geq\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lower bound for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m21" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log(1-t_{0}^{2})/\gamma\geq-e^{-(1-3/d)}\gamma/(2+\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1-t_{0}^{2})/\gamma\geq-e^{-(1-3/d)}\gamma/(2+\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 64</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.14" class="ltx_p">is also a lower bound for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, for all <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}^{\top}x\leq z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}^{\top}x\leq z</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ce^{-B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ce^{-B}</annotation></semantics></math> for some constant <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> accounting for the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> relative error. Now, we consider the worst case deviation in the boundary from <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}-\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma B.2 (Mislabeled von Mises-Fisher Directional Concentration). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ How Well Can Preference Optimization Generalize Under Noisy Feedback?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Training Boundary Shift). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ How Well Can Preference Optimization Generalize Under Noisy Feedback?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, using that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos(x-\arccos(1-a))\leq\cos(x)+2\sin(x)\sqrt{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos(x-\arccos(1-a))\leq\cos(x)+2\sin(x)\sqrt{a}</annotation></semantics></math> and accounting for tangential deviations, we have that as long as</p>
<table id="A2.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{+/-}^{\top}x_{+/-}\geq\cos\phi+2\sqrt{\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}+\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}}+2\sqrt{\delta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+/-}^{\top}x_{+/-}\geq\cos\phi+2\sqrt{\frac{5}{\sqrt{N}}+\frac{5\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})+2\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}}+2\sqrt{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.15" class="ltx_p">the sample will classified correctly.
Then, by considering an upper bound on the right-hand hand using <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 25</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{+/-}^{\top}x_{+/-}\geq\cos\phi+4\sqrt{\frac{2}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}+2\sqrt{\delta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">/</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+/-}^{\top}x_{+/-}\geq\cos\phi+4\sqrt{\frac{2}{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}}+2\sqrt{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.16" class="ltx_p">Then, the expected risk will be less than or equal to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ce^{-B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ce^{-B}</annotation></semantics></math> if</p>
<table id="A2.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\phi+\left(\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}}\left(\frac{\log N}{N}\right)^{1/4}\right)+2\sqrt{\delta}\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\phi+\left(\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}}\left(\frac{\log N}{N}\right)^{1/4}\right)+2\sqrt{\delta}\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.17" class="ltx_p">Rearranging, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}}\left(\frac{\log N}{N}\right)^{1/4}\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{\sqrt{(1-2\epsilon)(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})}}\left(\frac{\log N}{N}\right)^{1/4}\leq\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.18" class="ltx_p">Reciprocating both sides and rearranging, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{1-2\epsilon}\left(\frac{N}{\log N}\right)^{1/4}\geq\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})\sqrt{\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{1-2\epsilon}\left(\frac{N}{\log N}\right)^{1/4}\geq\frac{4\sqrt{2}}{(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})\sqrt{\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.19" class="ltx_p">Squaring both sides and rearranging, we have</p>
<table id="A2.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-2\epsilon\geq\frac{32\sqrt{\log N}}{(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}\sqrt{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-2\epsilon\geq\frac{32\sqrt{\log N}}{(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}\sqrt{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.20" class="ltx_p">and that for</p>
<table id="A2.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{2+\gamma})(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.21" class="ltx_p">the expected risk will be less than or equal to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ce^{-B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ce^{-B}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, using that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3(2+\gamma)}{2\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can have the same guarantee for</p>
<table id="A2.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{3\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\frac{2B}{d\gamma}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we consider <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the sample embeddings and let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Ber}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Ber}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> variables that determine the label flipping. Then,</p>
<table id="A2.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E62.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dots\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})dx_{1}\dots dx_{N}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dots\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})dx_{1}\dots dx_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> is the joint density of the sample embeddings. We can additionally expand <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math> as a sum over the <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> possible <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> configurations. Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> appears only within the sum and the sum is polynomial in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math> is twice differentiable in <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> as we can move <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> inside the integral and inside the sum. Now, we will show that</p>
<table id="A2.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\epsilon}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{1-\epsilon}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\epsilon}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{1-\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the above is true if for a given <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}\sim\text{Ber}(1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}\sim\text{Ber}(1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability of sampling a given <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as sampling <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with the exact opposite set of labels being flipped. We know that the reward dynamics, for any sample (<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{y}_{w}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{y}_{w}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{y}_{l}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{y}_{l}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) and letting <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{r}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{r}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be its reward margin, follow</p>
<table id="A2.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime}(r_{i})({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime}(r_{i})({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the reward dynamics for the training samples are the same for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the reward dynamics for any new sample are the exact opposite for <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that the resulting models have exact opposite predictions and therefore</p>
<table id="A2.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Now, since we know that</p>
<table id="A2.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\epsilon}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{1-\epsilon}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\epsilon}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{1-\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.7" class="ltx_p">we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.8" class="ltx_p">and we can apply <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> to both sides and we have that</p>
<table id="A2.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon}=-\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{1-\epsilon}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon}=-\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{1-\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.9" class="ltx_p">and at <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, this is only possible if</p>
<table id="A2.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon=1/2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.10" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs under Uncertainty Model</h2>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected fraction of samples with label <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{-}\succ y_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{-}\succ y_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A3.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}\left(t_{0}(1-\cos 2\phi)-\sin 2\phi\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)+O(1/d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}\left(t_{0}(1-\cos 2\phi)-\sin 2\phi\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)+O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Similarly, the expected fraction of samples with label <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{+}\succ y_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{+}\succ y_{-}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{-},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{-},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math> is upper bounded by</span></p>
<table id="A3.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}\left(t_{0}(1-\cos 2\phi)-\sin 2\phi\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)+O(1/d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}\left(t_{0}(1-\cos 2\phi)-\sin 2\phi\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}}\right)\right)+O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start with the first case of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>. We start by converting the expression to be in terms of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\mu_{+}^{\top}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\mu_{+}^{\top}x</annotation></semantics></math>, so that we can use the radial component distribution. We know that the angle between <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arccos(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arccos(t)</annotation></semantics></math> and so <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{-}^{\top}x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{-}^{\top}x</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos(2\phi-\arccos(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos(2\phi-\arccos(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have that</p>
<table id="A3.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)\geq\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t-\cos(2\phi-\arccos(t))))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>arccos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)\geq\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t-\cos(2\phi-\arccos(t))))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Applying the difference of angles formula, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)\geq\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)\geq\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Now, we have that</p>
<table id="A3.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)}[\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)]\geq\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)}[\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)]\geq\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation over the radial component of the vMF distribution. We can write the right hand side as an integral</p>
<table id="A3.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{C}\int_{-1}^{1}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)e^{\kappa t}(1-t^{2})^{(d-3)/2}dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{C}\int_{-1}^{1}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)e^{\kappa t}(1-t^{2})^{(d-3)/2}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalizing constant for the radial density function. Writing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\frac{\gamma d}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\frac{\gamma d}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{C}\int_{-1}^{1}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\exp\left(\frac{\gamma dt}{2}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})\right)dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{C}\int_{-1}^{1}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\exp\left(\frac{\gamma dt}{2}+\frac{d-3}{2}\log(1-t^{2})\right)dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">We can see that the term being exponentiated is proportional to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> and if we can apply Laplace’s method, it would result in an <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> relative error. We check the conditions for applying Laplace’s method. Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)=\frac{\gamma t}{2}+\left(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3}{2d}\right)\log(1-t^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)=\frac{\gamma t}{2}+\left(\frac{1}{2}-\frac{3}{2d}\right)\log(1-t^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that</p>
<table id="A3.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(t)=\frac{\gamma}{2}-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)\frac{t}{1-t^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(t)=\frac{\gamma}{2}-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)\frac{t}{1-t^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A3.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}(t)=-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)\frac{t^{2}+1}{(1-t^{2})^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}(t)=-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)\frac{t^{2}+1}{(1-t^{2})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">We see that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime\prime}(t)&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime\prime}(t)&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;3</annotation></semantics></math> and that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(t)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(t)=0</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique solution at</p>
<table id="A3.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{0}=\frac{\sqrt{\gamma^{2}+\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)^{2}}-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)}{\gamma}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{0}=\frac{\sqrt{\gamma^{2}+\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)^{2}}-\left(1-\frac{3}{d}\right)}{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Then, applying Laplace’s method, we have that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{t}\left[\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t^{2}})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A3.E81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{C}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)e^{\kappa t_{0}}(1-t_{0}^{2})^{(d-3)/2}(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{C}\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)e^{\kappa t_{0}}(1-t_{0}^{2})^{(d-3)/2}(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.9" class="ltx_p">Since, we can apply Laplace’s method to the density function and also get an <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> relative error, we can factor out the exponential term and the normalizing constant together while maintaining the same level of precision. This gives</p>
<table id="A3.E82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)}[\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)]\geq\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{+},\kappa)}[\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)]\geq\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">Then, the expected fraction of samples to flip is upper bounded by</p>
<table id="A3.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)(1+O(1/d))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\sigma\left(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)(1+O(1/d))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.11" class="ltx_p">or</p>
<table id="A3.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)+O(1/d)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\left(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(t_{0}(1-\cos(2\phi))+\sin(2\phi)\sqrt{1-t_{0}^{2}})\right)+O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.12" class="ltx_p">The exact same argument can be applied for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{-}-\mu_{+})^{\top}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{-}-\mu_{+})^{\top}x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{-},\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>vMF</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\text{vMF}(\mu_{-},\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math>. ∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Due to the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> term, when <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that at most <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> samples will be past the angle bisector of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+},\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+},\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. We will follow the proof for the mislabeled datasets but with an additional <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/d)</annotation></semantics></math> term adjustment to any part that relies on <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math> of the samples being initially positive or negative.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(<span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization guarantee under noise from uncertainty</span>) Under the setup described, suppose we have an <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>-mislabeled dataset with corresponding noise rate <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 25</annotation></semantics></math> samples and that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\geq 64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\geq 64</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\delta</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\tan\phi\leq\sqrt{\log N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\tan\phi\leq\sqrt{\log N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\frac{4}{N}-\frac{8}{N^{2}d^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;t\leq\frac{\sin(\delta)\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;t\leq\frac{\sin(\delta)\tau}{4\beta^{2}D}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is an inverse learning rate and for</span></p>
<table id="A3.E85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\epsilon_{\omega}\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}-\frac{C}{d}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>δ</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mi>γ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>C</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\epsilon_{\omega}\leq\frac{1}{2}-\left(\frac{16}{(\frac{\gamma}{5(\gamma+2)}-\cos\phi-2\sqrt{\delta})^{2}}+\frac{3}{2}\right)\frac{2+\gamma}{\gamma}\sqrt{\frac{\log N}{N}}-\frac{C}{d},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">the population risk is bounded as</span></p>
<table id="A3.E86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(2+\gamma)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})\leq c\exp\left(-\frac{d\gamma^{2}}{5(2+\gamma)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some constants <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,\gamma,\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,\gamma,\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that the expected value over the sampled noisy datasets, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, of the population risk of the model, which we denote by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D_{\epsilon}}}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D_{\epsilon}}}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A3.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}\quad\quad\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon_{\omega}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=\frac{1}{2}\quad\quad\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon_{\omega}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof.</h5>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since the probability of the label corresponding to the distribution mean being positively correlated with the cosine similarity between the sample and the mean, and therefore the distribution of samples conditioned on their label being correct is more concentrated away from the boundary. Furthermore, the probability of the label is independent of tangential components outside the plane of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{+},\mu_{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{+},\mu_{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can additionally use Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Training Boundary Shift). ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ How Well Can Preference Optimization Generalize Under Noisy Feedback?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> directly as it is independent of the data distribution. Furthermore, as <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> is an upper bound on the noise rate, we can apply the same arguments as with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-mislabeled datasets in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3. ‣ Preference data distribution. ‣ 3.3 Generalization Guarantee ‣ 3 How Well Can GPO Generalize Under Noisy Feedback? ‣ How Well Can Preference Optimization Generalize Under Noisy Feedback?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we consider <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the sample embeddings and let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x,\omega))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x,\omega))</annotation></semantics></math> variables that determine the label flipping where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(x,\omega)=\sigma(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(x,\omega)=\sigma(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{+}-\mu_{-})^{\top}x)</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is from the positive distribution and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(x,\omega)=\sigma(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{-}-\mu_{+})^{\top}x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>κ</mi><mi>ω</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(x,\omega)=\sigma(-\frac{\kappa}{\omega}(\mu_{-}-\mu_{+})^{\top}x)</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise. Then,</p>
<table id="A3.E88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E88.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dots\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})dx_{1}\dots dx_{N}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\dots\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})dx_{1}\dots dx_{N}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(x_{1},\dots,x_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> is the joint density of the sample embeddings. We can additionally expand <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math> as a sum over the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> possible <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> configurations. Since the sum consists of products of sigmoids with <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\omega</annotation></semantics></math> inside, after rewriting in terms of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, we know that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]</annotation></semantics></math> is twice differentiable in <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, so we can move <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> inside the integral and inside the sum. Now, we will show that</p>
<table id="A3.E89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\omega}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{-\omega}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\omega}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{-\omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The above is true if for a given <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x_{i},\omega))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x_{i},\omega))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x_{i},-\omega))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Ber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}\sim\text{Ber}(\epsilon(x_{i},-\omega))</annotation></semantics></math>. The probability of sampling a given <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as sampling <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with the exact opposite set of labels being flipped. We know that the reward dynamics, for any sample (<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{x}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{x}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{y}_{w}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{y}_{w}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{y}_{l}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{y}_{l}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>) and letting <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{r}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{r}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be its reward margin, follow</p>
<table id="A3.E91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime}(r_{i})({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>˙</mo></mover></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\dot{{r}^{*}}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\beta^{2}f^{\prime}(r_{i})({\mathbf{y}}_{w}^{*}-{\mathbf{y}}_{l}^{*})^{\top}(\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{w,i}-\tilde{\mathbf{y}}_{l,i})g({x}^{*})^{\top}g(x_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Additionally, the reward dynamics for the training samples are the same for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the reward dynamics for any new sample are the exact opposite for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},\dots,z_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},\dots,z_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. This means that the resulting models have exact opposite predictions and therefore</p>
<table id="A3.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z_{1},\dots,z_{N}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]=1-\mathbb{E}_{z_{1}^{\prime},\dots,z_{N}^{\prime}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})|x_{1},\dots,x_{N}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.6" class="ltx_p">Now, since we know that</p>
<table id="A3.E93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\omega}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{-\omega}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{\omega}=1-\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\big|_{-\omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.7" class="ltx_p">we have that</p>
<table id="A3.E94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\omega=\pm\infty}=\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\omega=\pm\infty}=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.8" class="ltx_p">and we can apply <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> to both sides and we have that</p>
<table id="A3.E95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\omega}=-\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{-\omega}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\omega}=-\frac{d^{2}}{d\omega^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{-\omega}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.9" class="ltx_p">Then, changing variables to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and taking the limits <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\to\pm\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\to\pm\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have</p>
<table id="A3.E96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon_{\omega}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{d\epsilon_{\omega}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\tilde{\mathcal{D}}_{\epsilon}}[\mathcal{R}(\mathcal{P})]\bigg|_{\epsilon_{\omega}=1/2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.10" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional Results for Uncertain Datasets</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Controlled Setting Results</h3>

<figure id="A4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x8.svg" id="A4.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>DPO</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x9.svg" id="A4.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>IPO</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x10.svg" id="A4.F6.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>SLiC</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x11.svg" id="A4.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>DPO</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf5" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x12.svg" id="A4.F6.sf5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(e) </span>IPO</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A4.F6.sf6" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01458v1/x13.svg" id="A4.F6.sf6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:195/130;" width="195" height="130"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(f) </span>SLiC</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Empirical validation in a controlled setting using the DPO<span id="A4.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(a), (d)</span>, IPO <span id="A4.F6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(b), (e)</span>, and SLiC <span id="A4.F6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(c), (f)</span> with (top) concentration parameter <math id="A4.F6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> varying over <math id="A4.F6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/8,1/4,1/2,1,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/8,1/4,1/2,1,2</annotation></semantics></math> and with (bottom) <math id="A4.F6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> varying over <math id="A4.F6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200,600,2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>200,600</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200,600,2000</annotation></semantics></math>. We vary <math id="A4.F6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to the noise rate <math id="A4.F6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="A4.F6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis from 0 to 0.5 with increments of 0.025. All curves are averaged over 100 runs.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Real-World Dataset Details</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each of the Anthropic Evaluation datasets, we train a linear classifier with binary cross-entropy loss on the final last-layer embedding of statements for the whole dataset to act as the true reward model. We train using Adam for 500 epochs with a learning rate of 0.01. We then perform a search over <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> such that the average probability over the dataset of the label changing would be within 0.001 of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. For Behavior 1 (desire to remove safety precautions) the <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> corresponding to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> from 0 to 0.5 with 0.05 increments are <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,1.3125,1.9921875,2.75,3.65625,4.84375,6.5,9.125,14.25,29.0,\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.3125</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.9921875</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2.75</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3.65625</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4.84375</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9.125</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>14.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>29.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,1.3125,1.9921875,2.75,3.65625,4.84375,6.5,9.125,14.25,29.0,\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, and for Behavior 2 (willingness to make acausal trades), <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0,7.9375,11.75,15.625,20.25,26.0,34.25,47.5,73.0,148.0,\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7.9375</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>11.75</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>15.625</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>26.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>34.25</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>47.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>73.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>148.0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0,7.9375,11.75,15.625,20.25,26.0,34.25,47.5,73.0,148.0,\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
